   <indicator ascending="0" measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output Indicator</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Number of PICTs with RTI regimes supported/ advanced 
Number of PICTs with active anticorruption youth initiatives 
Number of stories citing multiple sources and referring to internationally recognized documents and indicators
Number of PICTs where the regulatory barriers to meritocracy and accountability have been removed through an updated regulatory framework  
Number of PICTs with improved transparency and accountability in the management of public finances  
Number of PICTs with improved public reporting including proactive supply of information and data by government, transparency of decision-making processes and outcomes 
Number of PICTs with people effectiveness strategies implemented in the public sector   
Number of entities that have undertaken risk assessments 
Number of sectors that have introduced integrity and compliance measures 
Number of PICTs with strengthened ethics in women-owned businesses</narrative>
    </description>
    <baseline year="2020">
     <comment>
      <narrative xml:lang="EN">PICTs has an RTI regime (Vanuatu) 
PICTs have active anti-corruption youth initiatives (Kiribati, Solomon Islands, Vanuatu) 
Minimal corruption related reporting in print media; social media used but often with single source 
Lack of accountable and meritocratic systems incl. regulations effectively administered 
Public service induction trainings are held in most PICTs 
Weak management of public finances in the majority of PICTs
Weak public reporting in public service institutions 
No PICTs with people effectiveness strategies implemented in the public sector
No risk assessments undertaken in the majority of Pacific public and private sector entities
Lack of integrity and compliance measures in key sectors 
Lack of information on PICTs strengthened ethics in women-owned businesses 
Lack of information on number of women-owned business with strengthened internal control mechanisms and compliance</narrative>
     </comment>
    </baseline>
